meta {
  name: Create Pdf Catalog - Feature Not Enabled (422)
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/pdf-catalogs
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "WC Test PDF Catalog"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 422
  res.body.errors[0].description: contains pdfs
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-08 against "David's Dev Account". Creates
  nothing -- **this account does not have the PDF Catalogs feature
  enabled at all**:
  `{"data":[],"errors":[{"name":"ValidationError","description":"Cannot
  create new items the feature pdfs for account
  6a38f5a5b22478f30bfd755c"}]}`.

  This is a genuine account-level feature gate, not a request-shape
  problem -- the body itself (`name` only, matching
  `PdfCatalogCreateInputDto`'s single required field) is otherwise valid.
  **Blocks the rest of this phase**: no PDF catalog can be created in
  this account, so `output_attributes`/`pages`/`settings` remain
  completely untested, and Ecatalogs (Phase 4) will have no real
  `pdf_catalog_id` to reference -- document that field as
  optional/untestable-in-this-account rather than skip it silently. Flag
  to Plytix/the user: can this feature be enabled on "David's Dev
  Account" so PDF catalog creation can actually be tested?
}
